Z||000011||avengador1||12-11-2001||07:45 PM||||I'll keep an eye out for it. I work in Bridgeport. I bet it turns up in a couple of days, stripped. One of our friend's son had his Acura integra (all custom also) stolen from the Bowling alley in Orange and was recovered the next day minus all of the leather interior. The kid owed $9000 on the car and the insurance only gave him $6000 and change. His father thinks the inpound guy has another interior and made a deal with the insurance company (Allstate) so that they would not let him buy his car back.He had to take the money offered or pay for storage and have his title marked salvage by the insurance adjuster. He is going to file a complaint with the state about this. He probably would have been better off if the car was never recovered. Hope your sister has better luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Neal||12-11-2001||08:29 PM||||A few months back my sister (hmm everyones sister...) had her nissan 300ZX stolen.  She had it for a week, it was recovered minus the leather seats and a few dents on the hood.  Insurance company wrote it off payed out $16,000 she payed $12,000ish (CDN of course).<P>This is the kicker, the guy that sold her the car is under investigation for grand theft auto and insurance fraud.  My sister was the 3rd person that he sold and stole that car from in the last year...<P>Luckily she came out ahead on the whole thing, and i hope your sister gets her CRX back, or a nicer replacement.||||reg||1
