Z||000020||Jncomutt||12-12-2001||05:54 PM||||Well whadda ya know, the car turned up in Hartford.  The rims/tires are gone, the ignition was popped, and the interior is trashed.   We built a custom rear to it, so the 2 10" subs would be facing forward to replace the little "trunk" that was there.  It also had a fiberglass lift piece thing that we mounted the amps too, with the covers off of couse so you can see the inner workings.  This whole thing was 2 piece and attached right to the frame, well they cudn't figure how to get it out and destroyed it just enough to get the components.  The entire dash was smashed/removed.  I'm guessing they were trying to figure how to pop the hood.  We had disconnected the handle and put a short 5" cord that you must pull from underneath the front bumper to make it harder to get to.  Figured it would make it harder to disarm the alarm, and take the underhood goodies in a hurry.  (which worked, they never got it open)  Well needless to say, its being held until Monday for police investigation and evidence and such.  I'll letcha know how things work out with insurance and such...||||reg||1
